{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**The problem.** Given meeting time intervals `[start, end]`, return the **minimum number of conference rooms** needed so every meeting gets a room. A room freed at time 10 can host a meeting starting at 10."
    },
    {
      "type": "drawing",
      "src": "/drawings/ae6785aa-6266-430c-b824-615067e79828.svg",
      "alt": "Meetings 0 to 30, 5 to 10 and 15 to 20 on a timeline. At most two run at the same moment — 0 to 30 with 5 to 10, and later 0 to 30 with 15 to 20 — so two rooms are enough. Below, the start times sorted, 0, 5, 15, and the end times sorted, 10, 20, 30.",
      "width": 624,
      "height": 424,
