    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "[[0,30], [5,10], [15,20]]       ->  2\n[[7,10], [2,4]]                 ->  1\n[[1,10], [2,9], [3,8], [4,7]]   ->  4"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "The idea: count how many meetings overlap at the busiest moment"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The number of rooms needed is exactly the largest number of meetings **in progress at the same time**. And it doesn't matter *which* meeting ends — only *when* rooms free up. So the start times and the end times can be sorted **separately**: walk through the starts in order, and before each start, release every room whose meeting has already ended. The running count of rooms in use peaks at the answer."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "1. Brute force: count at every start"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The busiest moment always begins at some meeting's start. For each start, count the meetings running then."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function minMeetingRooms(intervals) {\n  let best = 0;\n  for (const [t] of intervals) {                     // the busiest moment starts at some meeting's start\n    let running = 0;\n    for (const [s, e] of intervals) if (s <= t && t < e) running++;\n    best = Math.max(best, running);\n  }\n  return best;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def min_meeting_rooms(intervals):\n    best = 0\n    for t, _ in intervals:                # the busiest moment starts at some meeting's start\n        running = sum(1 for s, e in intervals if s <= t < e)\n        best = max(best, running)\n    return best"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "int minMeetingRooms(int[][] intervals) {\n    int best = 0;\n    for (int[] m : intervals) {                       // the busiest moment starts at some meeting's start\n        int t = m[0], running = 0;\n        for (int[] o : intervals) if (o[0] <= t && t < o[1]) running++;\n        best = Math.max(best, running);\n    }\n    return best;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "int minMeetingRooms(vector<vector<int>>& intervals) {\n    int best = 0;\n    for (auto& m : intervals) {                       // the busiest moment starts at some meeting's start\n        int t = m[0], running = 0;\n        for (auto& o : intervals) if (o[0] <= t && t < o[1]) running++;\n        best = max(best, running);\n    }\n    return best;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(n²), space O(1).**"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "2. Sweep through start and end events"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Turn every meeting into two events: `+1` at its start, `−1` at its end. Sort the events by time — with ends before starts at the same time, so a freed room can be reused — and keep a running total."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function minMeetingRooms(intervals) {\n  const events = [];\n  for (const [s, e] of intervals) events.push([s, 1], [e, -1]);   // a start needs a room, an end frees one\n  events.sort((a, b) => a[0] - b[0] || a[1] - b[1]);              // at the same time, ends come first\n  let rooms = 0, best = 0;\n  for (const [, change] of events) {\n    rooms += change;\n    best = Math.max(best, rooms);\n  }\n  return best;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def min_meeting_rooms(intervals):\n    events = sorted([(s, 1) for s, _ in intervals] + [(e, -1) for _, e in intervals])   # ends sort first at a tie\n    rooms = best = 0\n    for _, change in events:\n        rooms += change\n        best = max(best, rooms)\n    return best"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "int minMeetingRooms(int[][] intervals) {\n    int[][] events = new int[intervals.length * 2][];\n    int k = 0;\n    for (int[] m : intervals) {\n        events[k++] = new int[]{m[0], 1};            // a start needs a room\n        events[k++] = new int[]{m[1], -1};           // an end frees one\n    }\n    Arrays.sort(events, (a, b) -> a[0] != b[0] ? Integer.compare(a[0], b[0]) : Integer.compare(a[1], b[1]));   // ends first at a tie\n    int rooms = 0, best = 0;\n    for (int[] ev : events) {\n        rooms += ev[1];\n        best = Math.max(best, rooms);\n    }\n    return best;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "int minMeetingRooms(vector<vector<int>>& intervals) {\n    vector<pair<int, int>> events;\n    for (auto& m : intervals) {\n        events.push_back({m[0], 1});                 // a start needs a room\n        events.push_back({m[1], -1});                // an end frees one\n    }\n    sort(events.begin(), events.end());              // pairs sort by time, then -1 before +1\n    int rooms = 0, best = 0;\n    for (auto& [time, change] : events) {\n        rooms += change;\n        best = max(best, rooms);\n    }\n    return best;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(n log n), space O(n).** This is a **sweep line**: process events in time order and track what's active."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "3. Two sorted arrays: starts and ends"
    },
    {
      "type": "simulator",
      "program": "meeting-rooms-ii",
      "caption": "Walk the sorted starts; before each one, free the rooms whose meetings have ended."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function minMeetingRooms(intervals) {\n  const starts = intervals.map((m) => m[0]).sort((a, b) => a - b);\n  const ends = intervals.map((m) => m[1]).sort((a, b) => a - b);\n  let rooms = 0, best = 0, j = 0;\n  for (let i = 0; i < starts.length; i++) {\n    while (ends[j] <= starts[i]) {   // a meeting ended before this one starts: its room is free\n      rooms--;\n      j++;\n    }\n    rooms++;                         // this meeting takes a room\n    best = Math.max(best, rooms);\n  }\n  return best;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def min_meeting_rooms(intervals):\n    starts = sorted(s for s, _ in intervals)\n    ends = sorted(e for _, e in intervals)\n    rooms = best = j = 0\n    for start in starts:\n        while ends[j] <= start:           # a meeting ended before this one starts: its room is free\n            rooms -= 1\n            j += 1\n        rooms += 1                        # this meeting takes a room\n        best = max(best, rooms)\n    return best"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "int minMeetingRooms(int[][] intervals) {\n    int n = intervals.length;\n    int[] starts = new int[n], ends = new int[n];\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        starts[i] = intervals[i][0];\n        ends[i] = intervals[i][1];\n    }\n    Arrays.sort(starts);\n    Arrays.sort(ends);\n    int rooms = 0, best = 0, j = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        while (ends[j] <= starts[i]) {   // a meeting ended before this one starts: its room is free\n            rooms--;\n            j++;\n        }\n        rooms++;                         // this meeting takes a room\n        best = Math.max(best, rooms);\n    }\n    return best;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "int minMeetingRooms(vector<vector<int>>& intervals) {\n    vector<int> starts, ends;\n    for (auto& m : intervals) {\n        starts.push_back(m[0]);\n        ends.push_back(m[1]);\n    }\n    sort(starts.begin(), starts.end());\n    sort(ends.begin(), ends.end());\n    int rooms = 0, best = 0;\n    size_t j = 0;\n    for (int start : starts) {\n        while (ends[j] <= start) {       // a meeting ended before this one starts: its room is free\n            rooms--;\n            j++;\n        }\n        rooms++;                         // this meeting takes a room\n        best = max(best, rooms);\n    }\n    return best;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(n log n), space O(n).** The `while` loop never runs past the end: by the time `starts[i]` is reached, at most `i` meetings can have ended. A **min-heap of end times** (see the Heap course) solves it the same way and also tells you which room each meeting gets."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Comparing the approaches"
    },
    {
      "type": "complexity",
      "rows": [
        {
          "approach": "Brute force: count at every start",
          "time": "O(n²)",
          "timeWhy": "At each of the **n** starts, count the meetings **running then**.",
          "space": "O(1)",
          "spaceWhy": "Just counters."
        },
        {
          "approach": "Sweep through start and end events",
          "time": "O(n log n)",
          "timeWhy": "**Sorting** the 2n events dominates; the sweep is O(n).",
          "space": "O(n)",
          "spaceWhy": "The list of **2n events**."
        },
        {
          "approach": "Two sorted arrays: starts and ends",
          "time": "O(n log n)",
          "timeWhy": "Two **sorts**, then one merge-like walk.",
          "space": "O(n)",
          "spaceWhy": "The two sorted arrays."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Edge cases to test"
    },
